  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "An object placed in front of a concave mirror at a distance of $x$ cm from the pole gives a 3 times magnified real image. If it is moved to a distance of $(x+5) \\mathrm{cm},$ the magnification of the image becomes 2 . The focal length of the mirror is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "zD1rX",
      "text": "$15 \\mathrm{cm}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "bNc4K",
      "text": "$20 \\mathrm{cm}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "yoDGV",
      "text": "$25 \\mathrm{cm}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "TaME8",
      "text": "$30 \\mathrm{cm}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given $y_{1}=3 x$ and $v_{2}=2(x+5)$ So here, Ist case\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{r}\r\n\\frac{1}{-x}+\\frac{1}{-3 x}=\\frac{1}{f} \\\\\r\n\\frac{1}{-(x+5)}+\\frac{1}{-2(x+5)}=\\frac{1}{f}\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$\r\nOn solving Eqs. (i) and (ii) we get $f=30 \\mathrm{cm}$",
